WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.800
Venom 2 is gonna be a scream well, almost.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.100
According to a new report by Deadline, Sony
Pictures has selected a second villain to

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:13.180
feature in the forthcoming Venom sequel, which
will be directed by Andy Serkis and star returning

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.780
actor Tom Hardy as the man possessed by the
titular symbiote.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.060
Deadline cites two sources with knowledge
of Venom 2 who have indicated that the Marvel

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.860
Comics villain Shriek will be a part of the
film's plot.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.579
With Shriek incorporated into the script,
the forthcoming Venom sequel slated to launch

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:34.020
in theaters on October 2, 2020 will feature
at least two infamous comic book villains.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.720
The first is Cletus Kasady, a serial killer
who serves as the host for the extraterrestrial

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.180
symbiote called Carnage.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.240
In the comics, Kasady is shipped off to Ryker's
Island Maximum Security Penitentiary after

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.690
murdering 11 people.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:51.020
There, he actually shares a cell with Eddie
Brock, who was incarcerated after wreaking

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.320
havoc across New York City as Venom.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.160
Kasady and Brock quickly form a deep hatred
for one another, with Brock despising Kasady

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.940
for killing people he knew were innocent and
helpless.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.440
Things take a horrifying turn when it's revealed
that Brock's symbiote Venom isn't dead but

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.480
merely dormant.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.480
When it reforms with Brock, it leaves a sort
of offspring stuck on Kasady.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.240
That entity turns into a full-fledged symbiote
of its own, bonds to Kasady, and becomes Carnage.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.240
In the first Venom film, these events play
out a little differently.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.640
Woody Harrelson is seen as Cletus Kasady in
a mid-credits scene, in which Eddie Brock

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.020
visits him in prison on an interview assignment.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.700
Kasady says the line that makes everyone say,
“OH!

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.900
That’s who the guy with the terrible wig
is!

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:37.820
"When I get outta here, and I will, there's
gonna be carnage."

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.540
Since it was basically a no-brainer that Carnage
would be in Venom 2, many fans speculated

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.160
that Shriek, Carnage's love interest, might
appear in the flick as well.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.640
Shriek's real name is Frances Louise Barrison,
and she made her print debut in May 1993's

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:57.060
Spider-Man Unlimited #1 during the Maximum
Carnage comic storyline.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:02.020
She's introduced as a drug dealer with a troubled
past who gets busted by the vigilante duo

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.920
Cloak and Dagger in the middle of one of her
drug runs.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.459
After being imprisoned in the Ravencroft Institute
for the criminally insane, getting shot in

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:14.120
the head by a police officer, and spending
time in Cloak's Darkforce Dimension, Frances

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.380
has a few screws loose.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.540
Her descent into insanity brings her latent
mutant abilities to the surface allowing her

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.090
to fly, manipulate sound, shoot sonic energy
blasts from her hands, and access others'

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.880
minds to manipulate their emotions and force
them to act violently.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:33.440
In the comics, Carnage meets Shriek as he's
breaking free from Ravencroft, where Shriek

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.600
is also being held.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:40.040
The two make their violent escape, team up,
embark on a gruesome killing spree, and create

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.720
a makeshift "family" with the villainous Carrion,
Demogoblin, and Doppelgänger.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.740
It's possible that Venom 2 may place Shriek
inside San Quentin Penitentiary, but still

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.840
see her meet Carnage when he's escaping.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.270
This would set up a fantastically frightful
storyline for the two villains, who may or

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.320
may not assemble a group of antagonistic pals
in the new movie.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.720
Perhaps a bigger question than how Shriek
will fit into the Venom 2 narrative is which

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.560
actress will fit into the role itself.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.420
There's no news yet, but Deadline's sources
say that Sony is primarily looking at unknown

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.960
actresses for the time being.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.820
Whoever ends up playing Shriek in Venom 2
will definitely share the screen with top

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:16.460
talent.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:21.660
In addition to starring opposite Woody Harrelson
as Carnage and Tom Hardy as Venom, the Shriek

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:26.400
actress will appear alongside Michelle Williams
as Anne Weying, Brock's ex-fiancée.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.670
Let's just hope that the lucky lady who lands
the role for Venom 2 will get to wear a better

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.000
wig than the wild one Harrelson sported in
the first Venom flick.

